 ## Headline metrics
+### Branded and non-branded are scored separately
+
+A **branded** prompt names the company or one of its aliases; a **non-branded**
+prompt describes a need with no company in mind. The tracker classifies every
+prompt automatically (override with `branded:` in the config) and reports the two
+buckets apart.
+
+This matters more than it sounds. AI cites a company back to itself almost every
+time it is asked about by name, so a blended rate is dominated by however many
+branded prompts happen to be in the set — add three branded prompts and the score
+rises without anything improving. **Lead with the non-branded rates.** They answer
+the question a client is actually paying to have answered: would AI recommend us
+to someone who has never heard of us?
+
+The blended figures are still reported, labelled as blended, so a number quoted
+from an earlier run can be reconciled. Never put one on the cover of a report.
+
 - **Citation rate** — % of answers that cite at least one brand-owned domain.
   The core AI-citation KPI: are you a *source*, not just a mention?
 - **Mention rate** — % of answers that name the brand (with or without a link).
